// Pull request author: einlamye
// Change: new rule
// Title: UAC Bypass Tool Spawning Shell - Odbcad32/Eudcedit
// Sigma ID: aa316e63-5945-4b42-a05f-d898c402f579
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, stealth, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the auto-elevating Windows binaries odbcad32.exe (ODBC Data Source Administrator) and
//   eudcedit.exe (Private Character Editor) spawning a command shell or scripting/proxy-execution
//   child process - a pattern indicative of a UAC bypass used to obtain a high-integrity process.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/odbcad32/
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Eudcedit/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8e7b36a9de00c979a098f16eb29c1c22fb63cb4b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_uac_bypass_odbcad32_eudcedit.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\odbcad32.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\eudcedit.exe") and (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\mshta.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe")
